    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prŏfātus</span></b> ,
		ūs (only in <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abl. sing.</i>), m.
			profor, <i>a speaking out</i>, <i>uttering</i>, <i>saying</i>, <i>pronouncing</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">effreno nimbos aequare profatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 3, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vocis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Apoc. 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voces dictu profatuque ipso tetrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 18, 11, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
